; AdaptiveMultiStrategyEA - commodity CFD account: gold trend sleeve + energy carry sleeve (chapter 107).
; Gold: same as AMS_Sleeves_Gold_Demo.set (hold gold while its close is above the 200-day average; 22.4% volatility; daily stop 4 x daily volatility).
; Energy carry sleeve (new): for USOIL and NATGAS, hold a position only when BOTH agree, reviewed every 7 days:
;     long  : the broker pays swap on longs  (futures curve in backwardation beyond the broker's cut) AND the close is above its 200-day average
;     short : the broker pays swap on shorts (curve in contango beyond the cut)                       AND the close is below its 200-day average
;   Size: each symbol's own volatility is 10% of equity per year. Daily stop at 4 x daily volatility. No specific days or times are used.
; Why: its profit is unrelated to the index dip-buying sleeve (correlation -0.08) and it was positive in 7-8 of 9 stock-market crash episodes.
;   Test on public futures data (EIA, WTI 1986-2024 and natural gas 1995-2024, broker cut 2.5% a year and spreads included):
;     Sharpe 0.39-0.41 (first half 0.59-0.63, second half 0.20); since 2009 about 0.2 - a modest edge, valuable mainly as a crash diversifier.
;     Added to the index sleeve at this size and scaled to the same maximum drawdown: crash-episode losses about half (-155% -> -69%, or -78..-90%
;     under stricter roll-day assumptions), worst year -13.7% -> -8..-11%, annual growth about the same (+21.2% -> +18.9..+22.6%).
; IMPORTANT: the MT5 tester applies TODAY's swap to all history, so this sleeve's profit CANNOT be verified in the tester (mechanics only).
;   The broker's swap history is unknown; reports/live_commodity/AMS_swaps.csv records it from now on.
; Attach to an XAUUSD chart (H1).
